  "conclusions": [
    "Qt 6.12.1 is a newly available fixed upstream route; a future isolated candidate can now be investigated using official Windows/source inputs.",
    "Installing PyQt6 6.12.1 from current PyPI metadata alone still selects native Qt 6.12.0, not fixed Qt 6.12.1. Binding and native runtime versions must be verified independently.",
    "Current PyQt6 6.12.1 requires Qt>=6.12,<6.13 and SIP>=13.13,<14; it cannot simply replace the current 6.11.0 binding while retaining the existing 6.11.3 native/SIP 13.11.1 inputs.",
    "Reviewed November 11-16 advisories affect modules absent from the recorded restricted profile. Reviewed retained Core/SVG advisories list fixed versions no later than 6.11.3. This is targeted triage, not comprehensive native security clearance.",
    "Keep the existing profile while completing independent MSVC staging/source mapping. A future 6.12.1 candidate must preserve exclusions and establish exact archives, native/source/SPDX correspondence, binding/plugin ABI and runtime validation before any canonical promotion."
  ],
